WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.233
Start continuity analysis with the process, not the server list.

00:00:04.233 --> 00:00:07.540
Identify which physical outputs and services are essential,

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:12.087
what minimum capacity is acceptable, how long interruption can be tolerated,

00:00:12.087 --> 00:00:16.220
and which conditions require safe shutdown rather than continued operation.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:19.940
Map each process to the assets that enable it.

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:22.007
PLCs and RTUs execute control.

00:00:22.007 --> 00:00:25.727
HMIs and SCADA systems provide operator visibility and commands.

00:00:25.727 --> 00:00:26.967
Historians preserve trends.

00:00:26.967 --> 00:00:29.860
Engineering workstations hold configuration and programming capability.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.340
Networks, time services, identity, remote access,

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:34.820
and security controls connect the environment.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.887
Dependencies extend beyond cyber assets.

00:00:36.887 --> 00:00:41.020
Electrical power, backup generation, cooling, compressed air, water, fuel, communications,

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:43.913
buildings, field instrumentation, spare parts, specialized tools,

00:00:43.913 --> 00:00:47.633
and trained personnel may determine whether recovery is possible.

00:00:47.633 --> 00:00:51.767
Vendor and supply-chain dependencies matter when equipment requires proprietary software,

00:00:51.767 --> 00:00:54.660
licenses, firmware, support credentials, or replacement modules.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:58.380
Record contract contacts, response times, shipping constraints, and alternatives.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:04.167
A spare is only useful if it is compatible and can be configured safely.

00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:09.127
Build a dependency map that shows prerequisites and single points of failure.

00:01:09.127 --> 00:01:14.087
A redundant server may still depend on one switch, one power source,

00:01:14.087 --> 00:01:16.567
one storage system, or one engineer.

00:01:16.567 --> 00:01:22.353
Include upstream and downstream processes so local recovery does not create a larger imbalance.

00:01:22.353 --> 00:01:26.487
Use the map to set restoration priorities and recovery packages.

00:01:26.487 --> 00:01:30.620
Validate it with operators, engineers, maintenance, safety, IT, security, facilities,

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:31.447
and vendors.

00:01:31.447 --> 00:01:35.580
Architecture documents should describe the system the organization actually operates,

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:39.300
then be updated after every significant change or exercise.
